 "title": "10 minute mein iPhone kaise? Dark Store ka khel | Case Study #shorts",
 "description": "10 minute mein iPhone kaise pahunchta hai? India ke quick commerce aur \"dark store\" model ki case study.\n\n- iPhone 18 Pro launch par ~10 minute delivery ka claim, BigBasket: pehle ghante 300+ units\n- Dark stores: ~7,800, 100+ shehar, ghar se 2-3 km\n- Users: 3 saal mein ~80 lakh se 6 crore+\n- Market: H1 2026 ~$9 arab, 2030 tak ~$50 arab (anumaan)\n\nSources:\nhttps://techcrunch.com/2026/09/18/in-india-the-new-iphone-can-arrive-faster-than-a-pizza/\nhttps://www.cbre.com/insights/reports/india-s-quick-commerce-scale-up-decoding-dark-stores-and-urban-logistics-demand\nhttps://www.finnovate.in/learn/blog/quick-commerce-india-2026-beyond-10-minute-delivery\n\nPhotos (Wikimedia Commons):\nFile:The Largest book warehouse of Finland 1974 (JOKABBL3B E39-2).tif | unknown | CC BY 4.0\nFile:Warehouse filled with stacked pallets showcasing efficient space usage during daytime operations.jpg | Shixart1985 | CC BY 2.0\nFile:FEMA - 24316 - Photograph by Liz Roll taken on 05-11-2006 in Texas.jpg | Liz Roll | Public domain\nFile:Instagram app on smartphone (grass background) (cropped).jpg | Santeri Viinamäki (both photo and screenshot) | CC BY-SA 4.0\nFile:Wikipedia app Nexus 4 in hand.JPG | Marcus Qwertyus | CC BY-SA 3.0\nFile:Brigade Road Bangalore.jpg | Amit | CC BY-SA 2.0\nFile:An urban road and traffic in Bangalore Karnataka India April 2014.jpg | Harsha K R from Bangalore, India | CC BY-SA 2.0\n\n#shorts #casestudy #quickcommerce #business #60seckhabar",
